{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## /rebar-debug RCA — CONFIRMED DEFECT, but repair is a DESIGN DECISION → ESCALATED (not auto-landed)\n\nInvestigated on a fresh worktree off `origin/main` @ `82a0d5cd328f`. Phase 1 (Understand) complete;\nPhase 2 (Repair) intentionally NOT entered — see disposition.\n\n### Confirmed mechanism (still present on current origin/main)\n`fsck` computes the \"issue count\" in TWO independent places that disagree for never-counted kinds:\n- **Exit code** — `_scan`'s counted tally, which respects each finding's `is_issue` flag:\n  `src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py:232-243` (`rc = 0 if issue_count == 0 else 1`) fed by\n  `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_tracker_health.py:58-71` (`issues += int(is_issue)`).\n- **`--output json`'s `issue_count`** — recomputed as `len(issues)` in `_transform_json`\n  (`src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py:143`), where `issues` is EVERY uppercase `KIND:` line matched by\n  the regex at `fsck.py:126`, with zero knowledge of `is_issue`.\n\nSo every never-counted kind (PUSH_PENDING, TRACKER_DIRTY_TMP_EVENT, WARN lines, STATUS_FORK_RESOLVED)\ninflates the JSON `issue_count` while contributing nothing to the exit code. `defect_legitimacy = defect`,\ncited against `docs/user-guide.md:455-460` (\"never counted … cannot by itself push fsck's exit code to 1\"),\nwhich is true of the exit code and false of the JSON payload users are pointed at.\n\n### Proof / verification (static + existing runtime pins)\n- Divergence is deliberately **test-pinned as today's contract**:\n  `tests/unit/test_unsigned_env_fsck_heldout.py:126` asserts `payload[\"issue_count\"] == len(payload[\"issues\"])`;\n  `tests/unit/test_doctor_dirty_tree.py:200-218` asserts `rc == 1` while `tracker_dirty_tmp_event`\n  sits inside `payload[\"issues\"]` (so it is in `issue_count` but not the exit code).\n- Not fixed since the report: the 3 post-floor commits touching fsck\n  (`44448546db6f` structured report for bug 326f, `6d95718080c8` CrossSessionWarning,\n  `1a589bdfc2a8` store resolution) leave `fsck.py:143` unchanged. No code commit references `29c3`.\n- Second sub-defect from the earlier comment reconfirmed present: `_missing_tracker_result`\n  (`fsck.py:246-267`) in JSON mode emits `{\"issues\":[],\"fixed\":[],\"issue_count\":0}` + exit 1 for an\n  UNINITIALISED store — byte-indistinguishable from a clean store; the diagnostic is text-path only.\n\n### Defect origin (attribution)\n`issue_count = len(issues)` decoupled from the counted tally was introduced by commit\n`56e130ff7132` \"feat(tier-e): port fsck in-process (E4)\" — ticket **scaly-bleat-haul** (Tier E, E4).\n(The `--output json` fsck shape itself was scoped under epic `dfa8` / story `42a0`.) Recorded here rather\nthan via `--caused-by` because the ticket is being escalated, not closed.\n\n### DISPOSITION: ESCALATE — hand the design decision to a human\nThis is a real defect, but the fix is NOT a mechanical repair a debugging agent may auto-land, because\nAC#1 is literally *\"Decide the meaning of `--output json`'s `issue_count`\"* and every plausible fix is a\n**schema-backed public-contract / output-format / vocabulary change**:\n- `issue_count` is a **required** field in `src/rebar/schemas/fsck.schema.json` (`required: [issues, fixed, issue_count]`);\n  changing its value/meaning changes observable output for existing JSON consumers.\n- The likely remedy (keep `issues[]` complete, redefine `issue_count` as the COUNTED subset, add a per-issue\n  `counted: bool`) adds **new output vocabulary** and would **deliberately invert an existing test-pinned\n  contract** (`test_unsigned_env_fsck_heldout.py:126`) — not a bug-fix edit but a semantics change.\n- The uninitialised-store sub-case needs its own decision (new `not_initialized` issue kind vs. reuse the\n  `compat_error` side channel), and `fsck_report()` in `src/rebar/_lib_reads.py` must keep failing closed.\n\n**Recommended (for the operator to approve, then run `rebar review-plan` on the class-level plan):**\nadopt the ticket's suggested design — `issues[]` stays complete; `issue_count` becomes the counted subset\n(agreeing with the exit code); add explicit per-issue `counted`; update `fsck.schema.json` + `docs/user-guide.md`;\nre-pin each never-counted kind; decide the uninitialised-store JSON payload separately. No fix has been written or pushed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787947655873455001,"uuid":"04fb8447-43bc-4d38-8d49-342c014cb276"}